2. Modified Version Identification

Anyone who modifies Lucid Drift and redistributes the modified version must clearly identify it as a modified version.

The modified version must not be presented as the original, official, or unmodified release of Lucid Drift.

The distributor must clearly indicate that the version has been modified and is not the official release maintained by the original author.

3. Modified Version Attribution

Anyone redistributing a modified version must identify themselves as the person or organization responsible for the modifications and redistribution.

The modified version must include a notice containing:

- The name of the original project: Lucid Drift.
- The name of the original author: Peyman.
- A link to the original repository.
- The name of the person or organization responsible for the modifications.
- A clear statement that the distributed version is modified and is not the official release.

4. Required Redistribution Notice

A modified version must include a notice substantially similar to the following:

